title: Brest-Litovsk
subtitle: The treaty, and the Left SRs.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: dix >= 28 and bol_regime = 1 and at_war = 1
priority: 40
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.at_war = 0;
RO.add(Q, {war_weariness: -20, army_discipline: 0, land_pressure: -5});
Q.lsr_left_gov = 1;
!}

= Brest-Litovsk

On 3 March the Soviet government signed the Treaty of Brest-Litovsk with Germany and her allies: Russia lost Poland, the Baltic provinces, Ukraine and a quarter of her population, and a third of her industry. Lenin had to threaten to resign to get it ratified: Trotsky's formula, "neither war nor peace", had failed and the Germans had advanced on Petrograd.

Martov and Kamkov, the Left SR leader, both spoke against ratification. The Left SRs left the government on 19 March, over the treaty; the Soviet Congress ratified the treaty by 784 votes to 261. The war with Germany is over, for now.

- @against: Martov speaks against ratification.
- @joint: Propose a joint defence programme with the Left SRs.
- @accept: Accept the treaty as a necessity.

@against
on-arrival: {!
RO.add(Q, {rel_lsr: 6, rel_bol: -2});
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', 2, -2);
RO.fac(Q, 'rightdef', 0, 5);
RO.boost(Q, {soldiers: 1, middle: 1});
!}

Martov spoke for the opposition: "the treaty is a shame, but your signing it is a disaster". It was the best speech of the Congress, and it was heard by nobody who mattered.

@joint
choose-if: rel_lsr >= 45
unavailable-subtitle: The Left SRs will not talk to us.
on-arrival: {!
RO.add(Q, {rel_lsr: 12, rel_bol: -3});
if (Q.ally_lsr < 1) { Q.ally_lsr = 1; }
RO.fac(Q, 'rightdef', 0, 5);
RO.fac(Q, 'defencist', 0, 3);
Q.anti_brest_front = 1;
!}

An anti-Brest front of Mensheviks and Left SRs has been formed, on paper. It has a common programme for a revolutionary defence: a people's militia, not a standing army, and a refusal to ratify.

@accept
on-arrival: {!
RO.add(Q, {rel_bol: 3, rel_lsr: -3});
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', 0, 8);
RO.fac(Q, 'defencist', 1, 0);
!}

We accepted the treaty as a fact. The Left SRs called it a betrayal of the revolution, and left the government.
